          text: 'A sun sign that never quite fit is the most common on-ramp to the big-three question, and the mismatch is real information \u2014 though rarely the kind it advertises. It usually means one layer is carrying a question built for three: the Sun is temperament, but instinct and presentation are separate angles, and a person is all three at once. The examinable version: name what the Sun description gets right, gets wrong, and misses entirely. That three-part list is the case for the Moon and the Rising \u2014 written in your own evidence rather than a framework\u2019s promise.'
