          text: 'The question behind the question is scope: is the trio an introduction or the conversation itself? The honest answer is that it depends on the question \u2014 a person question may need houses, aspects, and the rest of the planets; a social one may not need the trio at all. What doesn\u2019t work is letting the framework set the scope, because frameworks always answer \u201Cdeeper\u201D: there is no chart so complete that another consultation can\u2019t be sold on it. The examinable version: state the actual question you\u2019re carrying, then ask what evidence would answer it. If the answer is more placements, go deeper. If the answer is a decision you\u2019ve been postponing, more placements are a beautiful way to keep not making it.'
