        dontTell: 'This result can\u2019t name your color, or confirm that the field you\u2019re reading is objectively there \u2014 no quiz can; the emission is measurable, the perception is widespread, and the bridge between them is still an open question. What it also can\u2019t do is turn the snapshot into a system: even held honestly, a color readout is a lens on your state, not a measurement of it. What you can honestly examine is the pattern across time \u2014 and whether the readouts, checked against your actual weeks, have ever told you anything the quiet attention alone wouldn\u2019t have.',
