        negativePatternTip: {
          pattern: 'fact-hunting',
          text: 'fact-hunting is the most important failure mode here: the inquiry is aimed at recovering a verified fact \u2014 proof of who you were \u2014 or the session content is treated as a verdict on what happened. This is the one thing the practice cannot supply, and it is where regression does real harm. False memory is a documented risk, and session material cannot be distinguished from confabulation by how certain it feels; people have drawn conclusions about relationships and events from unverifiable content and acted on them. The honest correction is a change of question, not more caution inside the old one. Instead of &ldquo;who was I?&rdquo;, ask &ldquo;what is this pattern, and what would make it workable?&rdquo; The first has no answer anyone can verify and pulls you toward treating fiction as fact; the second is answerable, useful, and honest \u2014 and it is the question a good practitioner will steer you toward.'
        }
