          var s = 'Your answers describe the internal weather: the heaviness travels \u2014 it follows you into every room, which means the address was never the house. This is one of the most useful discoveries the cleansing question can produce, because it redirects everything: the same hour spent on smudging an innocent hallway is an hour not spent on the thing that\u2019s actually generating the weather. Internal heaviness has ordinary, workable sources: a season of stress, unprocessed grief, a decision postponed until it deafens, a mood that\u2019s been renting space long enough to feel structural.';
